name: Experimental advisory metadata does not complete Review or start default work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/chains_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 FINDINGS | metadata-findings
nav-mode:
keys: C
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 Finding-chain composition is experimental | experimental-shortcut
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/chains_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART before
ask: Does the shortcut explain experimental readiness and preserve ordinary findings without composing or starting work?
paste-file: @ART/run-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 candidate chain(s) | explicit-advisory-run
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/chains_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART after
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | advisory-receipt
ask: Does an explicit small metadata fold remain an advisory receipt with its original finding references, while the human ledger and investigation accounting stay unchanged?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: advisory-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: advisory-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: advisory-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: advisory-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | advisory-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: advisory-detail-40x12
ask: Can the recorded advisory outcome and details be read by paging at each size without changing verdicts, model or work?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | recovered-advisory
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/chains_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restart
ask: Does no-color restart retain the same advisory receipt and human decisions without a provider request or fresh Review completion?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
